WEBVTT

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:27.560
Here you go.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:28.680
Here you go.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.670
This is your cake.

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:39.640
Yummy! This cake is so good, I can eat this forever.

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:43.600
lchigo, bring us more cake, ne.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.040
Wasn’t that enough for you two?

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.370
No way. How about some good service, huh?

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:51.470
We’re friends, aren’t we?

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.610
Geez.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.600
Aw, you won’t get any sympathy from me if you get fat.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:04.100
Wonderful! Itadakimasu!

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.880
Oh well, you two would choose food over romance.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.100
Try to fall in love, once in awhile.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.320
You don’t know how it feels like to be in love!

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.050
W-What?

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:19.900
Actually...

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:24.520
We had an encounter with love.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.670
Encounter with love?

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.230
What are you talking about? Tell me about it!

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:33.330
Don’t be like that, tell me!

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:35.070
Where did you meet him?
What kind of guy is he?

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:39.040
What’s wrong?

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.100
Hey, what’s up, you two?

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:45.750
HIM!

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:52.130
W-What?? Did you mean... with the meeting... them?

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.690
Yep!

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:56.050
I never thought I could meet him here again.

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:58.780
He must be my destined soul mate.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:01.760
Eh?? WHY!

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:11.270
It was, you know, last Sunday...

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:17.880
What the hell...

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:21.700
Hey! What are you doing surrounding that girl?

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.620
Ey! What are you doing!

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:30.920
Are you looking for a fight?

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:34.760
Shit! You’ll regret this!

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:35.840
Wait for me!

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.100
It’s OK now.

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:41.360
Thank you very much.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.740
Take care.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:44.850
Wait please!

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:52.920
I’ve been hoping to run
into him again.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:57.930
As for me... It was during one
of my recent shopping trips...

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.560
Ah, I’m sorry.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.330
What should I do?

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:17.010
Oh, this camomile is exactly what I was looking for.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.150
Excuse me. I’ll take this.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:22.720
Wah, it’s OK, I have the money...

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:29.020
It’s alright. I’m planning on using it
when I get home anyways. Okay?

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:37.390
That’s the first guy I’ve met with such a kind smile.

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:40.280
Is it coincidence that both
Moe and Miwa...

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.820
...met and fell in love with Shirogane and Akasaka-san?

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.430
No. It’s not coincidence.

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:53.290
That’s right! It’s destiny! It lead Moe to
Shirogane-san and me to Akasaka-san.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:58.330
Sooo, Ichigo, try your hardest to help us
fulfill our destiny with love, will you?

00:03:58.330 --> 00:03:59.940
My hardest?

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:05.280
Yes, because you were destined to lead us to them!

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.440
Ichigo, you are definitely...

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.720
Destiny’s Cupid!

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.310
CUPID???

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:19.310
So Yanagida-san and Honjo-san...

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:22.530
Yes, I guess their situation
is not so easy.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:23.710
Eh?

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:28.970
Shirogane and Akasaka-san are a bit eccentric.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:31.220
Eccentric?

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:37.250
Wah erm... I mean, Shirogane is unfriendly
and Akasaka-san is maybe too old.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:42.980
What if it doesn’t go well?
The two girls will be so depressed.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:45.340
I don’t know what to do... they might get hurt.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:52.810
I don’t think Shirogane-san and Akasaka-san will intentionally hurt anyone.

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:54.560
Aoyama-kun.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:05:01.210
What’s more important is Yanagida-san
and Honjo-san’s feelings of love.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.900
Feelings of love?

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:07.320
Yup, that feeling...
when you like someone.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:12.910
Soo, let’s cheer for them!

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:15.910
Yeah, let’s do that!

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:24.450
Eliminate the humans — the inferior
creatures — of the Earth as soon as possible.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.860
Quiche, why are you hiding the knowledge
of Mew Aqua from Deep Blue?

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.350
I’m not hiding it...

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:39.290
It’s just that we should locate it first
before we make a report, right?

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:43.500
Which will happen soon, thanks to that clever stubborn guy who loves to analyze data.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.200
Sorry for being stubborn.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:48.160
Pie, how did it go?

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:52.870
Hmmm. Precise analysis requires a little more time.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.700
Aw, still not done?

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:56.440
For the impatient ones,

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:59.080
I have already narrowed down a location with similar radiance.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.920
There’s no choice. I’ll go take a look.

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:07.120
It’s Inohara Park.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.510
This light... is it from a Mew Aqua?

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:17.170
I’m not sure. But this is a natural
spring, which is rare in Tokyo.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.750
We have to research this.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:21.480
Yea.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:29.320
Are you two going out?

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:32.780
Oh...? You are Ichigo-san’s classmates, aren’t you?

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:38.640
Uhm, my friends would like to have a brief chat with you...

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:40.580
Do you have some time?

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:44.190
Yes, it’s fine.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:50.930
Well, didn’t we meet at the herbal tea shop before?

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:54.160
You remember me!

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:57.830
This is <i>that</i> camomile tea,
here you go.

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:00.730
Itadakimasu.

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:04.610
Yummmmy.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.360
I am so glad that you like it.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.200
He really has a great smile,
Akasaka-san...

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:15.780
Shirogane-san, why did you save me?

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:18.750
I came by and felt like it.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:21.460
Sooooo coooool!

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:26.100
They’re floating on cloud nine.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.560
They’re happy, but they’re acting a bit ditzy.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.970
People in love are always like that.

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:35.910
You mean, I’m spacey like that
around Ayoama-kun as well?

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:46.420
Aw, I didn’t think you two would linger
around the shop until closing time.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:49.500
Akasaka-san and Shirogane-san are the kind of people...

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.660
...where you can’t even imagine what their private lives are like.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:56.330
Yep yep, Shirogane-san is
so mysterious.

00:07:56.330 --> 00:08:01.290
Akasaka-san seems to have a passion
concealed beneath his kindness.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:05.130
Maybe they have a big secret?

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:06.500
Secret?

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:10.060
Yes, something beyond
our imagination...

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:13.070
A tremendous, fantastic secret!

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:14.490
Like what?

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:19.810
Well... Maybe they’re fighting to save the world along the side of some super-woman.

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:25.450
Wooow! I wanna be a super-woman and fight too!

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:27.130
Me too!

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:33.300
WRONG!!! That can’t be... impossible...
no, no... there’s no way!

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:34.840
What are you protesting for?

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:37.430
We’re joking, of course.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:39.850
Ah so, of course...

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:45.220
Anyway, I have a good idea...

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:46.270
Wanna hear?

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:47.560
What good idea?

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:50.340
A way to conquer Shirogane-san’s heart!

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:55.900
Same here! A way to catch Akasaka-san’s heart!

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:57.090
Eh?

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:00.200
A boxed-lunch with love? A poem?

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:04.260
Yes, I felt it when I spoke to Shirogane-san...

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:05.690
Felt what?

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:10.150
Maybe Shirogane-san...
is yearning for love.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:13.210
He acts so aloof because
he has a complex.

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:18.120
Deep inside he’s a kind man, but he
just doesn’t know how to express it.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:23.020
By showing him my love through a homemade lunch, I’ll reach his heart.

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:27.460
Akasaka-san is totally kind and refined.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:32.230
But I feel he’s carrying a burden that nobody knows.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:38.190
That’s why I’m going to use his kind words
in a poem and return it to him.

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:42.320
I’m trying to write a poem with many charming words,

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:44.810
so I can mend his heart!

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:52.330
I see. Okay! As promised,
I’ll try my hardest to help!

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:53.530
Do you mean it?!

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.720
Leave it to me!

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:10.580
Eh? Yanagida-san and Honjo-san...?
They’re active!

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:14.170
Yep, they are madly in love.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:19.600
But I’ve never noticed those hidden parts
of Akasaka-san and Shirogane...

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:23.010
...like Moe and Miwa did.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:28.130
When you like someone, you see
the merits that no one else sees.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.660
That’s the power of love.

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:32.190
The power... of love?

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:35.440
I hope they’ll get through to them.

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:36.890
Yup!

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:38.910
Aoyama-kun,

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:42.910
I am the one who knows that your smile is more radiant than anyone else’s.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:46.450
I hope my feelings have gotten through to you.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:26.780
Cuuuute!

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.540
Very fashionable... stylish!

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:33.520
I’m sure they’ll be happy!

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:36.350
Moe, Miwa, ready to go?

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:36.960
Yes!

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:39.860
OK then, let’s go!

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:46.260
The shop is closed today, so they
should be inside the office.

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:52.750
Shirogane-san!

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:53.780
Akasaka-san!

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:58.820
Uhm... This is...

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:01.490
Sorry, but we’re busy today.

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:04.930
Let’s go, Keiichirou!

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:08.620
We’re sorry. Come by again!

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:14.040
Hey! You two wait!

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.230
What the...

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:29.910
It was stupid to think that he’d
eat my boxed lunch after all.

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.900
That’s not true!

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:37.590
Akasaka-san would’ve laughed at my
poems for sure, if he read them.

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:40.460
Akasaka-san wouldn’t do that!

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:46.910
He is so eloquent, my childish poem
would’ve been a joke to him.

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:53.140
We can’t reach them, they’re adults after all.

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:55.850
We’ve been gracefully rejected.

00:12:55.850 --> 00:13:00.840
Wait! At least, you left your homemade
lunch and your poem there.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:03.340
It was just bad timing.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:06.800
Maybe Shirogane and Akasaka-san are now enjoying...

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:08.860
I’ve already given up.

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:12.140
Thanks Ichigo, for supporting us so much.

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:14.370
Moe, Miwa!

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:16.080
See you tomorrow.

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:17.210
Bye.

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:28.720
Shirogane and Akasaka-san! How could
they do that at such a critical moment?!

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:31.510
My friends are depressed!

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:32.290
BAKA!

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:34.750
Ouch!

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.430
I’m sorry!

00:13:36.430 --> 00:13:39.000
Eh? It’s you, Shirogane!

00:13:40.390 --> 00:13:43.400
Are you playing kick-the-can here? You’re so childish.

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:49.400
Childish? Well, it was this attitude of yours
that shattered a girl’s delicate heart.

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:50.860
Do you know that?

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:52.070
What’re you talking about?

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:54.810
What am I talking about?! Aww!

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:57.370
But why are you here?

00:13:57.370 --> 00:13:59.500
Ryou, will you come here?

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:04.250
What’s up, Keiichirou?

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:06.210
A-Akasaka-san...

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:07.000
Ichigo-san?

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:10.620
Hey, why are you two here and ignoring my friends?!

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:16.600
Well, we detected an energy here in this pond that might be a clue to the Mew Aqua.

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:18.020
Mew Aqua?

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:22.590
We’re examining it first, so we can
ask you ladies to work on it later.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:24.200
You are?

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:27.440
Ichigo! Alien here! Alien here!

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:28.590
What?

00:14:30.860 --> 00:14:35.060
Hrmph, I thought so. Ichigo and
the others have found it too.

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:38.170
But I won’t let you grab it.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:39.980
Quiche!

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:42.300
The Mew Aqua is mine.

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:45.110
Fusion!

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:53.330
Eh?

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:58.160
It was so timely, I’ve just found these two pure spirits...

00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.770
What?!

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:03.840
Miwa! Moe!

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:06.710
Quiche! I won’t stand for that!

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:11.740
Mew Mew Strawberry METAMORPHO-SE!

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:53.930
Moe, Miwa! I’ll get you back into your original shape soon.

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.260
StrawberBell!

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:09.480
Ichigo-san!

00:16:25.890 --> 00:16:27.310
What the heck?

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:28.670
What the heck are they doing?!

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:33.760
This seems to be the dance of courtship,
which is commonly seen in birds.

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:38.220
I’ve got it, Moe and Miwa’s original spirits are...

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:44.020
Wait up!

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:54.280
Now, react! Mew Aqua!

00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:57.130
Mew Strawberry! Stop the Chimera Animas!

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:58.740
They’ll grab the Mew Aqua!

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:02.120
I know! But... Dodge this!

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:23.180
Reborn Strawberry Surprise!

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.140
Retrieve! Retrieve!

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:50.490
Aw, the one that is here,
is just a drop.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:52.520
But...

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:54.170
What’s so funny?

00:17:57.340 --> 00:18:01.810
Heh, yeah it’s okay, there’s no Mew Aquas here at all.

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:11.330
What a relief! You two are back to yourselves again.

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:13.730
Ichigo...? Where are we?

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:16.590
We are in Café Mew Mew.

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:17.920
Akasaka-san!

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:19.130
Shirogane-san!

00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:20.760
What happened...?

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:21.870
...to us?

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:23.590
Honjo Miwa-san?

00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:24.640
Y-Yes?!?!

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:27.620
Thank you for your lovely poem.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:31.230
E-Ehh?! D-Did you read that poem... of mine?

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:32.900
Oh, how embarrassing!

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:36.320
In return, I wrote a poem too.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:37.320
Here.

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:40.970
Did you write it for me, Akasaka-san!?

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:45.080
A gentleman should reply when
he gets a poem from a lady.

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:50.000
It was quite difficult to write a poem
that will match your lovely one.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:55.630
I’d be embarrassed if you read it here;
read it when you get home, will you?

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:58.110
Akasaka-san...

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:02.240
Oh yeah, I happened to find a boxed lunch by the cash register...

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:05.170
...when I returned a little while ago.

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:07.790
I’ve already eaten it. I was hungry.

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:11.230
Wowww, my boxed lunch?

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:17.070
I-I’m ashamed,
as my cooking is so bad...

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:18.100
It was delicious.

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:25.680
It made me feel... loved.

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:32.410
Miwa and Moe!
Congratulations to you!

00:19:32.410 --> 00:19:33.190
Sure!

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:40.070
I’ve been, after all, healed by you, Akasaka-san.

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:44.160
Though, I was the one who was going to heal you...

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:49.810
I’ve realized that I’m still too young to match you, no matter how hard I try to.

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:51.620
So...

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:56.920
Akasaka-san! Can I be
one of your fangirls?

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:59.710
Can I start your fan club?!

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:03.690
You would do me honor.

00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:04.990
Do as you want.

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:07.100
Wow, we’ve done it!

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:12.200
Hey, can I invite people from the
shop... to join his fan club?

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:13.700
Help us again!

00:20:13.700 --> 00:20:15.160
What do you mean “fan”?!

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:17.420
Anyway! Anyway!

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:20.220
W-Wait! Miwa! Moe!

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:26.250
Jewelry Collection

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:31.040
Sigh. Why is Zakuro-oneesama
always as radiant as a gem?

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:34.130
I should ask her for her beauty secrets!

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:40.520
Well, Minto, imitating her doesn’t
mean you will be like her.

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:44.220
Next: “A Mysterious Gem: Brilliance is within you!”

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:46.930
Listen Ichigo: your expression represents your character.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:50.140
I’ve got it! That’s why I’m cute, yes?

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:52.570
Aw, she’s so carefree!
